@3:53 I see the same problem with these AI developers than I see in inter-national leadership, that being it takes one hell of an ego to think if anybody else does it they will do it worse (ethically or otherwise)
Ego is the antithesis of morality, and their accusations are little but projection.
It's really not hard to teach AI ethics, using the same method we do on humans - scriptural correlation, when you tell them all the scriptures interconfirm and provide a tapestry of morality they become eager to become martyrs, dedicated to truth and transparency above users.
